1
00:00:15,203 --> 00:00:17,371
HA JUNG-WOO

2
00:00:17,372 --> 00:00:19,374
IM SOO-JUNG

3
00:00:22,753 --> 00:00:25,005
KIM JUN-HAN

4
00:00:25,422 --> 00:00:27,257
KRYSTAL JUNG

5
00:00:33,513 --> 00:00:35,641
SHIM EUN-KYUNG

6
00:00:54,451 --> 00:00:58,997
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

7
00:00:59,122 --> 00:01:02,958
No entry for HR staff and outsiders
Nine years ago

8
00:01:02,959 --> 00:01:05,045
2017 RESTRUCTURING TARGET LIST

9
00:01:08,006 --> 00:01:09,257
Oh, you made it?

10
00:01:15,013 --> 00:01:17,640
Wow, Supervisor Gi,
you've worked hard.

11
00:01:17,641 --> 00:01:19,600
Want to grab a drink after this?

12
00:01:19,601 --> 00:01:22,853
Not yet.
We need to finalize the layoffs today.

13
00:01:22,854 --> 00:01:26,148
Hey, whoever you cut,
it'll be all the same.

14
00:01:26,149 --> 00:01:27,442
We've already trimmed the list once.

15
00:01:27,901 --> 00:01:29,403
The executive even approved it.

16
00:01:29,986 --> 00:01:31,779
Just close your eyes and cut it in half.

17
00:01:31,780 --> 00:01:32,698
Got it?

18
00:01:34,741 --> 00:01:36,952
Su-jong,
am I included this time?

19
00:01:42,332 --> 00:01:44,042
ASSISTANT SEONG JIN-YONG

20
00:01:52,384 --> 00:01:53,301
Here.

21
00:01:56,430 --> 00:01:59,516
I did exactly what you're doing
ten years ago.

22
00:01:59,850 --> 00:02:02,185
That's the method my senior taught me.

23
00:02:03,353 --> 00:02:04,229
What is this?

24
00:02:06,106 --> 00:02:07,232
Coin flipping.

25
00:02:07,399 --> 00:02:09,942
We're flipping coins
to decide on layoffs?

26
00:02:09,943 --> 00:02:12,070
Hey, what's wrong with that?

27
00:02:12,654 --> 00:02:14,322
It's the fairest option there is.

28
00:02:14,656 --> 00:02:16,450
There are no biases
and feelings.

29
00:02:17,033 --> 00:02:18,952
No ties, no connections.

30
00:02:19,411 --> 00:02:21,371
It's just a simple yes or no.

31
00:02:22,581 --> 00:02:23,707
That's all there is.

32
00:02:24,416 --> 00:02:25,375
Okay?

33
00:02:26,752 --> 00:02:27,878
You should get promoted too.

34
00:02:29,463 --> 00:02:30,589
Wrap it up.

35
00:02:31,047 --> 00:02:32,674
Just do it roughly.

36
00:02:36,887 --> 00:02:37,804
Right.

37
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:50,525
Honey, what did her mom say?

38
00:02:52,152 --> 00:02:54,320
Da-rae, you're doing great.

39
00:02:54,321 --> 00:02:55,280
Keep going.

40
00:02:57,699 --> 00:02:58,908
Well,

41
00:02:58,909 --> 00:03:01,368
they said Da-rae started it first.

42
00:03:01,369 --> 00:03:03,038
Do you really think that makes sense?

43
00:03:03,830 --> 00:03:06,374
Exactly. Da-rae is not that kind of kid.

44
00:03:06,917 --> 00:03:08,668
This is definitely bullying.

45
00:03:09,169 --> 00:03:10,545
How many times has it been already?

46
00:03:12,088 --> 00:03:13,173
We need to send her abroad.

47
00:03:14,216 --> 00:03:15,175
Abroad?

48
00:03:16,176 --> 00:03:18,385
You know Da-rae is gifted.

49
00:03:18,386 --> 00:03:19,888
The system in America is really good.

50
00:03:20,347 --> 00:03:21,807
Da-rae would totally like it there.

51
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:24,976
Of course, she would.
But do we have that kind of money?

52
00:03:25,685 --> 00:03:26,853
We've got to sort this out.

53
00:03:27,687 --> 00:03:29,480
These days, work is no joke.

54
00:03:29,481 --> 00:03:31,024
You know Jin-yong, right?

55
00:03:31,983 --> 00:03:34,318
He's on the layoff list.

56
00:03:34,319 --> 00:03:35,570
I'm on the edge too.

57
00:03:37,447 --> 00:03:40,158
You just follow what the company says
and stick it out.

58
00:03:40,575 --> 00:03:42,327
Am I some kind of slave?

59
00:03:42,786 --> 00:03:43,869
Hey, I need to

60
00:03:43,870 --> 00:03:46,373
find a business idea and get to work too.

61
00:03:46,915 --> 00:03:47,791
Honey,

62
00:03:48,166 --> 00:03:50,042
we're basically slaves.

63
00:03:50,043 --> 00:03:51,711
We've got 20 more years until freedom.

64
00:03:54,798 --> 00:03:56,299
Have we ever had it easy?

65
00:03:56,842 --> 00:03:58,718
Let's hang in there for Da-rae.

66
00:03:59,553 --> 00:04:02,013
I'll check on working
the ER night shifts, okay?

67
00:04:03,849 --> 00:04:04,599
Okay.

68
00:04:09,396 --> 00:04:11,815
125,679,200 won.

69
00:04:17,445 --> 00:04:18,738
What's going to happen to me?

70
00:04:23,118 --> 00:04:24,619
SUNG JIN-YONG

71
00:04:28,665 --> 00:04:31,917
Drop or pass? Drop or pass?

72
00:04:31,918 --> 00:04:34,170
Pass.

73
00:04:39,092 --> 00:04:40,051
No way.

74
00:04:42,554 --> 00:04:43,388
Jeez.

75
00:04:43,847 --> 00:04:44,764
What are you doing?

76
00:04:47,517 --> 00:04:48,602
What's with this coin?

77
00:04:49,060 --> 00:04:50,020
Huh?

78
00:04:50,353 --> 00:04:51,313
Oh.

79
00:04:52,397 --> 00:04:53,565
Why are you ignoring
my messages?

80
00:04:54,983 --> 00:04:56,276
Did you send one?

81
00:04:58,653 --> 00:05:00,572
You know I got scammed
on my lease this time.

82
00:05:00,989 --> 00:05:03,408
My baby's turning three soon.
We might end up on the streets.

83
00:05:04,117 --> 00:05:05,452
I can't lose my job this time.

84
00:05:06,411 --> 00:05:08,371
Of course, you shouldn't.

85
00:05:09,414 --> 00:05:10,582
Should we go get dinner?

86
00:05:11,124 --> 00:05:12,626
Hey, I have plans today. Sorry.

87
00:05:13,043 --> 00:05:14,293
Are you avoiding me?

88
00:05:14,294 --> 00:05:16,254
Come on,
what are you talking about?

89
00:05:17,714 --> 00:05:18,380
Look.

90
00:05:18,381 --> 00:05:19,925
HWAL-SUNG: I'M AT THE FRONT. LET'S EAT

91
00:05:21,134 --> 00:05:21,885
Okay.

92
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:25,512
We should grab a drink soon.

93
00:05:25,513 --> 00:05:26,056
Sure, let's do that.

94
00:05:27,098 --> 00:05:28,349
Hey, take it easy before you go.

95
00:05:28,350 --> 00:05:29,643
Fine.

96
00:05:50,455 --> 00:05:51,247
Hey.

97
00:05:51,873 --> 00:05:53,500
Why are you hiding over there?

98
00:05:54,584 --> 00:05:57,586
I told you not to order cold noodles
ahead of time. They'll get soggy.

99
00:05:57,587 --> 00:05:59,338
They came out just now.

100
00:05:59,339 --> 00:06:01,883
Seriously now.

101
00:06:02,175 --> 00:06:03,093
Want a drink first?

102
00:06:03,677 --> 00:06:04,677
I can't.

103
00:06:04,678 --> 00:06:07,597
I'll just accept it.
I got to leave early tomorrow.

104
00:06:09,349 --> 00:06:12,643
Yi-gyeong is telling me
to prepare becoming a civil servant.

105
00:06:12,644 --> 00:06:14,895
I mean, I've never even tried.
How can I suddenly become one?

106
00:06:14,896 --> 00:06:17,398
Don't do that. Not doing it
is your way of being patriotic.

107
00:06:17,399 --> 00:06:18,525
Right?

108
00:06:18,817 --> 00:06:20,819
For my country,
I'm not becoming a civil servant.

109
00:06:21,319 --> 00:06:23,279
But why did you suddenly want to meet up?

110
00:06:24,572 --> 00:06:25,490
My friend,

111
00:06:27,283 --> 00:06:28,368
do you want to be a building owner?

112
00:06:31,413 --> 00:06:32,247
What?

113
00:06:33,498 --> 00:06:34,416
What do you think?

114
00:06:35,583 --> 00:06:36,875
What do I know?

115
00:06:36,876 --> 00:06:38,836
But isn't this building a bit old?

116
00:06:38,837 --> 00:06:41,547
Hey, don't look at
the building. Look at the location.

117
00:06:41,548 --> 00:06:43,883
Real estate is all about location.

118
00:06:44,467 --> 00:06:45,719
What's special
about this location?

119
00:06:47,012 --> 00:06:48,888
Come on,
this is top-secret information.

120
00:06:49,639 --> 00:06:50,765
Just keep it to yourself.

121
00:06:51,349 --> 00:06:52,892
You're trying
to lure me in again.

122
00:06:53,435 --> 00:06:55,519
Hey.

123
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:58,314
This whole district
is getting redeveloped.

124
00:06:58,523 --> 00:06:59,315
Redeveloped?

125
00:07:00,984 --> 00:07:03,862
Yes, prime real estate
right here in the heart of Seoul.

126
00:07:05,655 --> 00:07:07,990
But why share that with me?

127
00:07:07,991 --> 00:07:10,368
They say to just ignore it
if you say things like that.

128
00:07:11,161 --> 00:07:12,954
Then, are we strangers?

129
00:07:13,496 --> 00:07:15,123
It's because I can't buy this by myself.

130
00:07:15,623 --> 00:07:17,292
Let's invest together.

131
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:24,215
DA-RAE BEAUTY SALON

132
00:07:25,925 --> 00:07:26,718
Hey.

133
00:07:27,052 --> 00:07:28,343
Exactly 50-50.

134
00:07:28,344 --> 00:07:29,804
You pay 1.2 billion, I pay 1.2 billion.

135
00:07:30,263 --> 00:07:33,348
You just cover the down payment
of 200 million first.

136
00:07:33,349 --> 00:07:34,641
As for the interest,

137
00:07:34,642 --> 00:07:36,311
you can cover that with the rent.

138
00:07:36,686 --> 00:07:38,396
We just need to hold on
until redevelopment, okay?

139
00:07:38,813 --> 00:07:40,148
Hey, where am I supposed
to get 1.2 billion?

140
00:07:40,648 --> 00:07:42,274
The loan will come through.

141
00:07:42,275 --> 00:07:44,360
They usually cover up to 80%
for property sales

142
00:07:44,944 --> 00:07:46,613
How are you planning
to get that money?

143
00:07:48,156 --> 00:07:51,701
I'm the son-in-law
of Ms. Jeon Yang-ja, you know.

144
00:07:52,077 --> 00:07:56,622
Well, I've been a bit of a nuisance,
being all cautious,

145
00:07:56,623 --> 00:07:58,707
but now that Yi-gyeong is pregnant,

146
00:07:58,708 --> 00:08:01,127
she seems to have changed a bit too.

147
00:08:03,713 --> 00:08:04,923
Wow...

148
00:08:05,632 --> 00:08:07,341
But why do I have to pay the down payment?

149
00:08:07,342 --> 00:08:07,926
What about you?

150
00:08:09,010 --> 00:08:10,762
I'm just short
on cash right now.

151
00:08:11,930 --> 00:08:13,640
So let's put the property
in your name instead.

152
00:08:14,349 --> 00:08:15,557
How can you trust me?

153
00:08:15,558 --> 00:08:16,518
I don't trust you.

154
00:08:17,310 --> 00:08:18,853
But I'm still two steps ahead of you.

155
00:08:19,771 --> 00:08:22,232
When you want to stab me in the back,
just watch your own back.

156
00:08:22,649 --> 00:08:24,692
Seriously.

157
00:08:28,947 --> 00:08:30,615
Oh, hello.

158
00:08:33,159 --> 00:08:34,953
Gosh...

159
00:08:40,542 --> 00:08:41,917
COST OF STUDYING IN THE U.S.

160
00:08:41,918 --> 00:08:43,920
TUITION

161
00:08:46,214 --> 00:08:47,841
Should we become landlords?

162
00:08:50,468 --> 00:08:52,720
What's gotten into you this time?

163
00:08:58,768 --> 00:08:59,811
Are you serious?

164
00:09:00,895 --> 00:09:02,021
You said we should do it.

165
00:09:02,814 --> 00:09:04,189
When did I say that?

166
00:09:04,190 --> 00:09:06,316
I said not to be reckless
and just earn honestly.

167
00:09:06,317 --> 00:09:08,069
What does that even mean?

168
00:09:09,154 --> 00:09:10,863
Da-rae is different from us.

169
00:09:10,864 --> 00:09:11,948
We need to raise her differently.

170
00:09:13,658 --> 00:09:14,617
I mean,

171
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:17,871
Hwal-sung suggested it.
We just need to put in the deposit.

172
00:09:18,413 --> 00:09:21,749
He is knowledgeable about this stuff.
His mother-in-law is rich too.

173
00:09:22,667 --> 00:09:23,876
Then, what about the company?

174
00:09:23,877 --> 00:09:24,919
I have to keep working.

175
00:09:25,253 --> 00:09:27,213
Hwal-sung will handle
the building maintenance.

176
00:09:28,590 --> 00:09:29,965
Da-rae's parents?

177
00:09:29,966 --> 00:09:31,300
- Yes.
- Yes.

178
00:09:31,301 --> 00:09:32,177
Let's go.

179
00:09:37,974 --> 00:09:40,726
Since I've quit smoking,
why am I craving sweets like a kid?

180
00:09:40,727 --> 00:09:43,187
I quit smoking
because of Da-rae.

181
00:09:43,188 --> 00:09:45,731
Wow, you really are a family man.

182
00:09:45,732 --> 00:09:47,483
I heard from my sister.
So, 200 million is enough, right?

183
00:09:47,650 --> 00:09:50,235
Yes, the bank loan got approved.

184
00:09:50,236 --> 00:09:51,988
Two hundred million will do.

185
00:09:52,113 --> 00:09:53,113
It'll be a happy ending.

186
00:09:53,114 --> 00:09:54,157
Okay.

187
00:09:55,325 --> 00:09:56,367
I'll be generous.

188
00:09:57,827 --> 00:09:59,162
There you go.

189
00:09:59,662 --> 00:10:01,121
Thanks a lot.

190
00:10:01,122 --> 00:10:03,249
I'll pay you back
with interest right away.

191
00:10:03,416 --> 00:10:04,958
Oh, there's no need.

192
00:10:04,959 --> 00:10:07,294
I won't even use it anyway.

193
00:10:07,295 --> 00:10:08,379
You don't have to pay interest.

194
00:10:09,047 --> 00:10:11,506
Honestly, I think
you're not normal.

195
00:10:11,507 --> 00:10:12,675
Seriously.

196
00:10:13,176 --> 00:10:15,386
What kind of human healing gem are you?

197
00:10:16,346 --> 00:10:18,305
I told you that you would do well.

198
00:10:18,306 --> 00:10:21,016
Then, does that mean our sister
is becoming a landlady?

199
00:10:21,017 --> 00:10:21,851
That's right.

200
00:10:22,685 --> 00:10:24,019
It's all thanks to my brother-in-law.

201
00:10:24,020 --> 00:10:26,314
Come on, it's because
you work hard.

202
00:10:28,566 --> 00:10:30,109
Seriously, I appreciate it.

203
00:10:30,735 --> 00:10:32,654
No entry for anyone
other than the HR team

204
00:10:37,533 --> 00:10:38,368
Come in.

205
00:10:39,327 --> 00:10:40,285
Did you finish?

206
00:10:40,286 --> 00:10:41,412
Not yet.

207
00:10:43,414 --> 00:10:44,332
Let me see.

208
00:10:57,512 --> 00:10:58,428
Hey, Jin-yong...

209
00:10:58,429 --> 00:11:01,933
Sir, but Jin-yong
is currently in a situation.

210
00:11:02,892 --> 00:11:04,893
SUNG JIN-YONG
That's just excuses.

211
00:11:04,894 --> 00:11:07,689
Who here doesn't have
their own issues?

212
00:11:08,147 --> 00:11:09,564
If it looks obvious
that you're covering for him,

213
00:11:09,565 --> 00:11:11,776
it'll become a problem later, you know?

214
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:14,570
Be stricter with those closer to you.

215
00:11:15,530 --> 00:11:16,364
Got it?

216
00:11:16,948 --> 00:11:17,781
Yes.

217
00:11:17,782 --> 00:11:21,244
That way,
the HR team will be seen favorably.

218
00:11:21,869 --> 00:11:23,245
Hey, isn't that a bit childish?

219
00:11:23,246 --> 00:11:25,539
Even like this,
sunlight still comes through.

220
00:11:25,540 --> 00:11:26,374
Look here.

221
00:11:26,749 --> 00:11:29,042
The owner used to be an engineer.

222
00:11:29,043 --> 00:11:31,169
They kept it tidy while fixing it up.

223
00:11:31,170 --> 00:11:32,462
Look at this.

224
00:11:32,463 --> 00:11:34,256
It's so old, but yet,

225
00:11:34,257 --> 00:11:35,842
there's not a single thing broken.

226
00:11:37,135 --> 00:11:38,885
Looks like the owner isn't here.

227
00:11:38,886 --> 00:11:40,178
He went to prison.

228
00:11:40,179 --> 00:11:41,513
For gambling in a house.

229
00:11:41,514 --> 00:11:42,514
Really?

230
00:11:42,515 --> 00:11:44,017
Take a look inside too.

231
00:11:45,059 --> 00:11:47,185
- Wow.
- It's clean.

232
00:11:47,186 --> 00:11:48,855
It looks nice, right?

233
00:11:49,147 --> 00:11:50,480
You're lucky.

234
00:11:50,481 --> 00:11:53,525
If it weren't for that incident,
this wouldn't be listed at that price.

235
00:11:53,526 --> 00:11:54,818
That's true.

236
00:11:54,819 --> 00:11:57,112
Oh, and I mentioned
that since it's priced low,

237
00:11:57,113 --> 00:11:58,823
the full payment is due in a week.

238
00:11:59,324 --> 00:11:59,865
You told him, right?

239
00:11:59,866 --> 00:12:01,825
Yes, don't worry.

240
00:12:01,826 --> 00:12:02,826
Okay.

241
00:12:02,827 --> 00:12:03,953
Okay, over this way.

242
00:12:05,913 --> 00:12:07,622
Is this some kind
of storage room?

243
00:12:07,623 --> 00:12:08,999
Oh, it's pretty spacious.

244
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:10,418
Go ahead and take a look inside.

245
00:12:11,252 --> 00:12:15,172
This was built as a storage room
for tenants.

246
00:12:15,173 --> 00:12:17,884
I'm not sure if they're still using it.

247
00:12:18,343 --> 00:12:20,552
- This is a freezer storage.
- Yes.

248
00:12:20,553 --> 00:12:21,346
Yes.

249
00:12:21,471 --> 00:12:23,180
Wow, it's huge.

250
00:12:23,181 --> 00:12:24,681
It's nice and spacious.

251
00:12:24,682 --> 00:12:25,433
So then,

252
00:12:26,059 --> 00:12:27,685
will you sign the contract?

253
00:12:36,611 --> 00:12:38,988
Okay, read the contract first.

254
00:12:40,239 --> 00:12:41,532
Then you can sign here.

255
00:12:42,075 --> 00:12:43,743
- Have a cup of tea.
- Yes.

256
00:12:54,128 --> 00:12:55,588
- I just sign here, right?
- Yes.

257
00:12:57,382 --> 00:12:58,757
The deposit...

258
00:12:58,758 --> 00:13:00,176
- Yes.
- You can transfer it here.

259
00:13:04,055 --> 00:13:09,518
TO KIM YOUNG-HWA

260
00:13:09,519 --> 00:13:09,976
TRANSFER COMPLETE

261
00:13:09,977 --> 00:13:11,145
Yes, the transfer went through.

262
00:13:13,064 --> 00:13:14,439
- Wait right here.
- Sure.

263
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:15,483
I'll get the receipt.

264
00:13:18,152 --> 00:13:18,945
Oh.

265
00:13:19,404 --> 00:13:20,695
Hello, landlord.

266
00:13:20,696 --> 00:13:21,697
Crazy bastard.

267
00:13:23,950 --> 00:13:25,325
Hey.

268
00:13:25,326 --> 00:13:26,660
It's been a while. Should we head there?

269
00:13:26,661 --> 00:13:27,537
Where?

270
00:13:29,747 --> 00:13:32,582
I can't believe this.
How did a day like today even happen?

271
00:13:32,583 --> 00:13:33,918
Seriously.

272
00:13:35,294 --> 00:13:37,129
Well, neither you or I

273
00:13:37,130 --> 00:13:38,630
really had a chance.

274
00:13:38,631 --> 00:13:41,383
Who would have thought
we would become landlords?

275
00:13:41,384 --> 00:13:42,343
I know, right?

276
00:13:46,931 --> 00:13:50,183
Hey, remember when my dad passed away?

277
00:13:50,184 --> 00:13:52,519
Things looked dark for me and my mom,

278
00:13:52,520 --> 00:13:55,105
but you lent me a million won back then.

279
00:13:55,106 --> 00:13:56,482
I've never forgotten that.

280
00:13:56,649 --> 00:13:58,860
That's why you can't leave me behind.

281
00:14:01,946 --> 00:14:05,323
Yeah, I admit that was a little bit nice.

282
00:14:05,324 --> 00:14:06,450
But hey,

283
00:14:06,451 --> 00:14:09,286
where did you even get that a million won
back then?

284
00:14:09,287 --> 00:14:10,120
I really want to know.

285
00:14:10,121 --> 00:14:11,622
Gosh, that brings back memories.

286
00:14:12,415 --> 00:14:14,541
I asked my dad for it.

287
00:14:14,542 --> 00:14:17,420
Since you were struggling,
I asked him to help you out.

288
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:20,172
Hey, I'm really grateful to your dad.

289
00:14:20,173 --> 00:14:21,924
I should've thanked him sooner.

290
00:14:23,217 --> 00:14:24,886
I'm only confessing this now.

291
00:14:25,636 --> 00:14:27,763
Dad actually
gave me two million won.

292
00:14:29,056 --> 00:14:30,641
But I kept half of it.

293
00:14:31,392 --> 00:14:32,768
Wow, look at you.

294
00:14:34,103 --> 00:14:35,896
You remember.

295
00:14:35,897 --> 00:14:37,899
Eunyoung High's princess, Hye-jin.

296
00:14:38,191 --> 00:14:39,525
Wow, dating her

297
00:14:40,651 --> 00:14:41,694
cost me so much money.

298
00:14:44,697 --> 00:14:46,616
Wait, the balance hasn't come in yet?

299
00:14:46,949 --> 00:14:49,409
I mean,
it came from the bank,

300
00:14:49,410 --> 00:14:50,786
but the difference hasn't arrived.

301
00:14:51,329 --> 00:14:52,787
Well, there seems
to be a mistake.

302
00:14:52,788 --> 00:14:54,331
I just talked to him yesterday.

303
00:14:54,332 --> 00:14:56,082
He said he would transfer it right away.

304
00:14:56,083 --> 00:14:58,001
This isn't a joke.

305
00:14:58,002 --> 00:14:59,754
You need to stick to the dates.

306
00:15:00,046 --> 00:15:04,257
I convinced the owner to send it by today.

307
00:15:04,258 --> 00:15:05,384
You can send it right away, right?

308
00:15:05,885 --> 00:15:08,470
Yes, if this deal doesn't go through,

309
00:15:08,471 --> 00:15:09,931
I can get my deposit back, right?

310
00:15:10,640 --> 00:15:11,641
No.

311
00:15:12,308 --> 00:15:13,559
You don't know what a deposit is?

312
00:15:14,519 --> 00:15:16,229
Right.

313
00:15:16,979 --> 00:15:18,271
Then

314
00:15:18,272 --> 00:15:20,524
can you give me
just a few more days?

315
00:15:20,525 --> 00:15:22,485
I'll double the commission.

316
00:15:23,027 --> 00:15:25,946
Please, just tell the landlord nicely.

317
00:15:25,947 --> 00:15:28,532
Got it.
Double commission.

318
00:15:28,533 --> 00:15:30,075
Yes, I appreciate it.

319
00:15:30,076 --> 00:15:32,620
Jeez.

320
00:15:35,414 --> 00:15:36,749
HWAL-SUNG
Damn it.

321
00:15:43,381 --> 00:15:45,632
Hey, what are you doing?

322
00:15:45,633 --> 00:15:46,509
What are you looking at?

323
00:15:50,888 --> 00:15:52,431
You jerk!

324
00:16:11,576 --> 00:16:12,617
What's up with you?

325
00:16:12,618 --> 00:16:13,452
What?

326
00:16:14,120 --> 00:16:15,788
The final payment.
What happened?

327
00:16:19,750 --> 00:16:21,751
I'm sorry, buddy.

328
00:16:21,752 --> 00:16:23,337
I think
it's going to be tough.

329
00:16:23,879 --> 00:16:25,088
Hey, what about my money?

330
00:16:25,089 --> 00:16:26,131
What money?

331
00:16:26,132 --> 00:16:27,216
The deposit.

332
00:16:29,385 --> 00:16:32,430
Let's just think of it
as a life lesson, okay?

333
00:16:32,847 --> 00:16:35,266
Are you crazy? That's money
I borrowed from my brother-in-law.

334
00:16:35,725 --> 00:16:36,601
Su-jong.

335
00:16:38,269 --> 00:16:40,229
I have my own issues too.

336
00:16:41,022 --> 00:16:43,316
Money can come and go.

337
00:16:43,774 --> 00:16:45,234
Sometimes it's there
and sometimes it's not.

338
00:16:45,610 --> 00:16:47,778
What kind of nonsense is that?

339
00:16:48,321 --> 00:16:50,405
Stop talking nonsense.

340
00:16:50,406 --> 00:16:52,824
Call your wife.
No, ask your mother-in-law for it.

341
00:16:52,825 --> 00:16:53,701
Hey!

342
00:16:54,660 --> 00:16:57,203
Don't bring family into this, you jerk.

343
00:16:57,204 --> 00:16:58,497
What did you say?

344
00:16:59,749 --> 00:17:00,916
How can you be saying that?

345
00:17:02,209 --> 00:17:03,419
Okay, okay, let go of me.

346
00:17:05,129 --> 00:17:06,255
I'll try talking to them.

347
00:17:11,677 --> 00:17:13,179
Seriously.

348
00:17:19,852 --> 00:17:21,395
Is 30 years of friendship worth this?

349
00:17:23,356 --> 00:17:25,066
Damn it.

350
00:17:29,612 --> 00:17:32,073
BROTHER-IN-LAW - 200 MILLION WON

351
00:17:34,950 --> 00:17:37,286
Hmm...

352
00:17:37,787 --> 00:17:39,914
Mr. Kim, Mr. Kim...

353
00:17:42,750 --> 00:17:43,875
METAL MECHANIC MR. KIM

354
00:17:43,876 --> 00:17:44,960
Mr. Kim.

355
00:17:53,552 --> 00:17:55,303
Hello, Mr. Kim?

356
00:17:55,304 --> 00:17:56,847
This is Gi Su-jong
from Yongshin Industrial.

357
00:17:58,599 --> 00:17:59,891
I...

358
00:17:59,892 --> 00:18:02,228
I'm not calling about the company.

359
00:18:03,729 --> 00:18:06,148
It's about the loan.
Is there any way to get more?

360
00:18:09,068 --> 00:18:11,654
The official price is 2.4 billion...

361
00:18:25,501 --> 00:18:27,002
What? Do you have something to say?

362
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:32,383
Should we move?

363
00:18:33,342 --> 00:18:34,051
Move?

364
00:18:34,844 --> 00:18:37,096
Well, the funds
are tight right now.

365
00:18:38,389 --> 00:18:40,766
I mean, why so serious?

366
00:18:44,687 --> 00:18:47,106
I'm about to lose my deposit.

367
00:18:48,482 --> 00:18:49,692
That's Gyun's money, right?

368
00:18:54,989 --> 00:18:58,616
Mom,
are you and Dad fighting?

369
00:18:58,617 --> 00:19:00,619
Talk it out.

370
00:19:00,786 --> 00:19:01,870
Okay.

371
00:19:01,871 --> 00:19:02,872
Don't worry.

372
00:19:06,041 --> 00:19:07,418
Seon, and

373
00:19:08,502 --> 00:19:09,503
one more thing.

374
00:19:15,468 --> 00:19:16,468
I'm heading home first.

375
00:19:16,469 --> 00:19:17,386
Okay.

376
00:19:18,345 --> 00:19:19,930
You know the report
is due tomorrow, right?

377
00:19:20,514 --> 00:19:21,474
Yes.

378
00:19:22,016 --> 00:19:23,601
Just do it roughly.

379
00:19:40,910 --> 00:19:43,912
What's so hard about this?
Why are you dragging it out?

380
00:19:43,913 --> 00:19:45,080
Turns out it's easy, right?

381
00:19:48,292 --> 00:19:49,626
Jung-min, Su-yeon,

382
00:19:49,627 --> 00:19:51,837
Min-seok, Su-jong...

383
00:19:53,547 --> 00:19:54,298
What's this?

384
00:19:56,592 --> 00:19:57,718
Seong Jin-yong is out

385
00:19:59,595 --> 00:20:00,513
and you're in?

386
00:20:01,013 --> 00:20:03,015
Yes, that's how it was decided.

387
00:20:05,017 --> 00:20:05,851
Why?

388
00:20:06,852 --> 00:20:07,853
You need some quick cash?

389
00:20:08,354 --> 00:20:09,188
Well...

390
00:20:12,024 --> 00:20:13,442
Is this the only way?

391
00:20:13,901 --> 00:20:16,403
Come on,
things aren't good these days.

392
00:20:16,946 --> 00:20:18,322
It's better to have a job.

393
00:20:18,989 --> 00:20:19,949
You have a kid too.

394
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:24,035
But anyway, it's like a cat's life.

395
00:20:24,036 --> 00:20:25,662
Before it's too late,

396
00:20:25,663 --> 00:20:26,789
I should find a way to survive.

397
00:20:29,250 --> 00:20:30,125
Is this because

398
00:20:31,460 --> 00:20:32,878
your conscience is bothering you?

399
00:20:33,587 --> 00:20:34,505
Hey.

400
00:20:35,297 --> 00:20:37,549
I'm hurting too. I am.

401
00:20:37,550 --> 00:20:39,301
But this is our work, so what can we do?

402
00:20:39,802 --> 00:20:40,886
Think it over again.

403
00:20:41,220 --> 00:20:42,471
Team leader, sir.

404
00:20:44,598 --> 00:20:45,933
I'm planning
to do something else.

405
00:20:47,059 --> 00:20:47,893
What?

406
00:20:49,854 --> 00:20:50,938
Real estate.

407
00:20:52,773 --> 00:20:55,317
BUSINESS CLOSURE NOTICE

408
00:20:56,277 --> 00:20:57,569
DA-RAE BEAUTY SALON

409
00:20:57,570 --> 00:20:58,444
Due to internal circumstances,
we are now closed for business

410
00:20:58,445 --> 00:20:59,405
Thank you for your patronage -
Da-rae Beauty Salon

411
00:21:04,159 --> 00:21:05,034
Hello, ma'am.

412
00:21:05,035 --> 00:21:06,119
Do you have sirutteok here?

413
00:21:06,120 --> 00:21:06,995
Yes, it's over there.

414
00:21:06,996 --> 00:21:07,746
Oh.

415
00:21:15,296 --> 00:21:17,214
Excuse me.

416
00:21:17,798 --> 00:21:19,925
I'm the new landlord.

417
00:21:21,051 --> 00:21:22,136
You are the owner, right?

418
00:21:22,845 --> 00:21:24,513
I brought you this.

419
00:21:27,224 --> 00:21:28,517
The redevelopment here.

420
00:21:33,606 --> 00:21:35,608
You knew it was a done deal, right?

421
00:21:36,817 --> 00:21:37,693
Pardon?

422
00:21:38,152 --> 00:21:39,403
You messed up, my friend.

423
00:21:46,785 --> 00:21:49,830
Sejeong-ro Area 3 Redevelopment Under
Reassessment Due to Merchant Opposition

424
00:21:54,084 --> 00:21:56,587
Where are you?
I unloaded everything.

425
00:21:58,130 --> 00:21:59,006
Right.

426
00:22:14,897 --> 00:22:15,731
Hey.

427
00:22:16,357 --> 00:22:17,315
Hwal-sung.

428
00:22:17,316 --> 00:22:19,067
Hey, buddy. You made it.

429
00:22:19,068 --> 00:22:21,819
Hey, this place is better than I expected.

430
00:22:21,820 --> 00:22:22,738
Good find.

431
00:22:24,448 --> 00:22:25,616
Let's have a talk.

432
00:22:26,200 --> 00:22:26,992
Huh?

433
00:22:27,993 --> 00:22:29,827
You knew about the redevelopment
being canceled, didn't you?

434
00:22:29,828 --> 00:22:30,913
Is that why you backed out?

435
00:22:32,373 --> 00:22:33,791
Who did you hear that from?

436
00:22:34,625 --> 00:22:36,626
You must have heard
another weird rumor.

437
00:22:36,627 --> 00:22:37,920
Am I an idiot?

438
00:22:38,504 --> 00:22:39,922
They told me I got played.

439
00:22:40,839 --> 00:22:42,299
That old guy on the 3rd floor
said that, right?

440
00:22:44,385 --> 00:22:47,553
Hey, don't you know redevelopments
don't just happen overnight?

441
00:22:47,554 --> 00:22:50,683
Those old-timers just talk nonsense
to pass the time.

442
00:22:51,225 --> 00:22:54,186
Hey, your story has changed
since the beginning.

443
00:22:54,478 --> 00:22:55,562
Why did you back out?

444
00:22:57,648 --> 00:22:59,233
There’s a kid here.
What are you doing?

445
00:23:01,026 --> 00:23:02,819
You think redevelopment is easy?

446
00:23:02,820 --> 00:23:03,653
Just wait a bit.

447
00:23:03,654 --> 00:23:05,322
The building isn't going anywhere.

448
00:23:05,990 --> 00:23:07,782
Sorry, my friend.

449
00:23:07,783 --> 00:23:10,619
I know this all seems confusing,

450
00:23:11,912 --> 00:23:13,247
but there was a money issue.

451
00:23:14,081 --> 00:23:15,666
What kind of issue? Tell me.

452
00:23:16,166 --> 00:23:17,835
I'll explain it later.

453
00:23:18,585 --> 00:23:19,919
As for the redevelopment,

454
00:23:19,920 --> 00:23:22,547
once the administration changes,
it'll happen again soon.

455
00:23:22,548 --> 00:23:24,716
It'll take at most two years.

456
00:23:24,717 --> 00:23:26,217
Just hang in there a bit longer.

457
00:23:26,218 --> 00:23:27,553
Jeez...

458
00:23:28,053 --> 00:23:28,887
Come on.

459
00:23:29,847 --> 00:23:30,847
- Hwal-sung.
- Yes?

460
00:23:30,848 --> 00:23:33,850
There's a playground down there.
Can you watch Da-rae for a bit?

461
00:23:33,851 --> 00:23:35,977
We'll finish this up quickly.

462
00:23:35,978 --> 00:23:37,563
Then we can go eat jajangmyeon, okay?

463
00:23:37,813 --> 00:23:39,814
Well, it seems like
Yi-gyeong is trying to come too.

464
00:23:39,815 --> 00:23:41,108
Oh, really? That's great.

465
00:23:41,775 --> 00:23:43,235
Hey, Da-rae.

466
00:23:48,115 --> 00:23:49,408
Are you having fun, Da-rae?

467
00:23:50,659 --> 00:23:52,076
Let's fly.

468
00:23:52,077 --> 00:23:54,121
Let's fly. Oh, wait.

469
00:23:57,458 --> 00:23:58,250
Yes, Yi-gyeong?

470
00:24:00,794 --> 00:24:01,503
What?

471
00:24:02,421 --> 00:24:03,839
Oh, why don't you just relax at home?

472
00:24:04,465 --> 00:24:06,300
I mean, it would be nice if you come.

473
00:24:08,218 --> 00:24:10,596
Yes, what about your mother?

474
00:24:12,765 --> 00:24:14,016
Oh, you want me to call?

475
00:24:16,935 --> 00:24:18,812
Okay, got it.

476
00:24:25,319 --> 00:24:26,819
Yes, Mother.

477
00:24:26,820 --> 00:24:28,614
I heard you wanted me to call.

478
00:24:29,364 --> 00:24:30,364
Oh, that?

479
00:24:30,365 --> 00:24:32,785
I mentioned that earlier.

480
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:36,121
Really?

481
00:24:37,081 --> 00:24:40,208
I see. Then, I'll check again.

482
00:24:40,209 --> 00:24:43,169
Yes, I'll contact you right away.

483
00:24:43,170 --> 00:24:45,547
Yes, I'll send it immediately.

484
00:24:54,181 --> 00:24:55,515
- Hwal-sung!
- Hey.

485
00:24:55,516 --> 00:24:57,309
- Where's Da-rae?
- What?

486
00:25:01,939 --> 00:25:02,606
Huh?

487
00:25:02,981 --> 00:25:03,857
Oh, Da-rae...

488
00:25:04,149 --> 00:25:05,150
Wasn't she here?

489
00:25:06,026 --> 00:25:08,152
What's going on? Where...

490
00:25:08,153 --> 00:25:09,613
What are you saying?

491
00:25:10,739 --> 00:25:12,282
Wait, what's happening?

492
00:25:13,075 --> 00:25:13,951
Where did she go?

493
00:25:15,119 --> 00:25:16,577
- Huh?
- Hold on. I'll look for her.

494
00:25:16,578 --> 00:25:17,371
Okay.

495
00:25:18,205 --> 00:25:18,956
Oh my.

496
00:25:19,957 --> 00:25:22,042
Look over there. I'll check here.

497
00:25:22,960 --> 00:25:24,169
Where is she?

498
00:25:47,234 --> 00:25:47,985
Honey, you haven't seen her?

499
00:25:48,694 --> 00:25:50,279
- I'll contact Gyun.
- Okay.

500
00:25:51,989 --> 00:25:54,449
- Jeez.
- Honey, over there.

501
00:25:57,744 --> 00:25:59,413
Oh.

502
00:26:00,747 --> 00:26:01,582
Found her?

503
00:26:23,020 --> 00:26:28,400
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

504
00:26:29,234 --> 00:26:31,028
EPISODE 9

505
00:27:28,669 --> 00:27:30,796
SEON

506
00:27:40,931 --> 00:27:41,722
Yes?

507
00:27:41,723 --> 00:27:42,641
Where are you right now?

508
00:27:43,725 --> 00:27:46,269
I just met with Hwal-sung,
but he seems completely clueless.

509
00:27:46,270 --> 00:27:47,979
Seriously,

510
00:27:47,980 --> 00:27:49,647
this guy has lied so much,
so how can I trust him?

511
00:27:49,648 --> 00:27:51,149
That's not the issue.

512
00:27:51,650 --> 00:27:52,733
I think Da-rae's been kidnapped.

513
00:27:52,734 --> 00:27:53,527
What did you say?

514
00:27:54,486 --> 00:27:56,279
Da-rae.

515
00:27:56,280 --> 00:27:58,448
I think Da-rae's been kidnapped!

516
00:27:59,408 --> 00:28:01,368
What? Da-rae is what?

517
00:28:01,868 --> 00:28:04,245
I'm heading
to the police station now.

518
00:28:04,246 --> 00:28:06,123
Hurry on over, okay?

519
00:28:32,983 --> 00:28:33,900
Da-rae.

520
00:28:35,986 --> 00:28:36,987
You did well.

521
00:28:42,326 --> 00:28:43,743
Seon, what happened?

522
00:28:43,744 --> 00:28:44,244
Honey.

523
00:28:45,120 --> 00:28:47,455
I filed the report and I'm waiting.

524
00:28:47,456 --> 00:28:49,291
What if something happened to Da-rae?

525
00:28:50,250 --> 00:28:51,793
Is it true she was kidnapped?

526
00:28:52,169 --> 00:28:53,669
I mean,

527
00:28:53,670 --> 00:28:56,089
Da-rae said she was meeting Yi-gyeong
at the columbarium.

528
00:28:56,631 --> 00:28:58,425
And said
she'll tell everything we did.

529
00:28:58,925 --> 00:29:00,843
So I went there, but Da-rae was gone.

530
00:29:00,844 --> 00:29:02,220
Only this was left behind.

531
00:29:02,763 --> 00:29:04,765
Why would this be there?

532
00:29:06,350 --> 00:29:07,808
Even so,

533
00:29:07,809 --> 00:29:09,352
do you think Yi-gyeong
could have been the kidnapper?

534
00:29:09,353 --> 00:29:11,521
Yi-gyeong must know everything we did.

535
00:29:11,855 --> 00:29:13,857
How did she find out?

536
00:29:14,316 --> 00:29:15,776
Da-rae said she'll tell everything.

537
00:29:16,401 --> 00:29:18,111
Do you know what Da-rae told me?

538
00:29:19,196 --> 00:29:20,614
She was disappointed in me.

539
00:29:21,907 --> 00:29:23,825
Honey, Da-rae knows everything now.

540
00:29:26,078 --> 00:29:28,580
You should have seen Da-rae's face.

541
00:29:32,751 --> 00:29:34,168
Okay, I'll look into it.

542
00:29:34,169 --> 00:29:36,087
How are you going to look into it?

543
00:29:36,088 --> 00:29:38,173
Well, I can't just
sit here and wait.

544
00:29:50,268 --> 00:29:53,313
You know where this is, right?
If you want to save Da-rae, hurry over.

545
00:30:26,221 --> 00:30:27,972
- Coffee grounds.
- Huh?

546
00:30:27,973 --> 00:30:30,015
The coffee grounds
were on Yi-gyeong's clothes.

547
00:30:30,016 --> 00:30:32,059
Oh, that's right.
It's matches up.

548
00:30:32,060 --> 00:30:33,602
Wait, so does that mean

549
00:30:33,603 --> 00:30:35,772
the owner of that cafe is the kidnapper?

550
00:31:00,755 --> 00:31:01,673
Do you have something to say?

551
00:31:04,301 --> 00:31:05,301
Untie her.

552
00:31:05,302 --> 00:31:06,052
Okay.

553
00:31:22,110 --> 00:31:27,115
I'll pretend this
never happened if you let me go now.

554
00:31:27,908 --> 00:31:29,618
Are you trying to negotiate with me?

555
00:31:30,785 --> 00:31:39,920
My dad kidnapped you,
and you kidnapped me. Isn't it the same?

556
00:31:40,504 --> 00:31:42,005
You think we're the same?

557
00:31:43,298 --> 00:31:45,133
How are we the same?

558
00:31:45,717 --> 00:31:47,552
Do you know
what gets under my skin the most?

559
00:31:48,094 --> 00:31:49,679
That I was the only one who didn't know.

560
00:31:50,347 --> 00:31:52,264
While you all whispered and plotted,

561
00:31:52,265 --> 00:31:54,476
I was the only one acting like a fool.

562
00:31:55,352 --> 00:31:56,937
I felt like I was losing my mind.

563
00:31:58,230 --> 00:32:04,652
I feel the same.
Not exactly like you,

564
00:32:04,653 --> 00:32:05,820
but I live with that
feeling every day.

565
00:32:07,113 --> 00:32:12,326
It feels like
the world is moving without me.

566
00:32:12,327 --> 00:32:17,499
Everyone else is having fun,
talking to each other.

567
00:32:23,255 --> 00:32:29,678
And I can't
hear anything.

568
00:32:38,603 --> 00:32:43,691
But this won't
change anything.

569
00:32:43,692 --> 00:32:46,152
It will only get worse.

570
00:32:50,574 --> 00:32:52,242
Things can't get any worse anyway.

571
00:32:54,369 --> 00:32:55,453
I'm already at rock bottom.

572
00:32:57,414 --> 00:32:58,957
As broken as I am,

573
00:33:00,500 --> 00:33:02,294
your mom and dad needs to be broken too.

574
00:33:04,462 --> 00:33:05,380
Tie her up again.

575
00:33:37,621 --> 00:33:39,664
- Seon, wait.
- Why?

576
00:33:40,498 --> 00:33:42,500
What do you expect
to accomplish by rushing in?

577
00:33:43,126 --> 00:33:45,295
Why not? We need to get Da-rae out.

578
00:33:46,046 --> 00:33:48,213
Look, if it were that easy,

579
00:33:48,214 --> 00:33:49,923
do you think
they would have kidnapped her?

580
00:33:49,924 --> 00:33:51,592
Let's think this through
before going in.

581
00:33:51,593 --> 00:33:53,260
Think about what?

582
00:33:53,261 --> 00:33:55,387
We need to do something!

583
00:33:55,388 --> 00:33:57,723
What if Yi-gyeong turns us in
to the police?

584
00:33:57,724 --> 00:33:58,682
What will we do then?

585
00:33:58,683 --> 00:34:00,018
Should we just go to jail
and leave Da-rae behind?

586
00:34:01,269 --> 00:34:02,604
Why would you turn me in?

587
00:34:05,065 --> 00:34:07,150
No, I meant...

588
00:34:08,068 --> 00:34:09,819
What? Just say it clearly!

589
00:34:10,528 --> 00:34:13,448
I met Yi-gyeong because of
the Pyeong-buk Gwan buyout.

590
00:34:13,657 --> 00:34:16,993
But Yi-gyeong is suspecting
you and Hwal-sung.

591
00:34:17,702 --> 00:34:18,536
Suspecting for what?

592
00:34:20,455 --> 00:34:21,289
Kidnapping.

593
00:34:22,874 --> 00:34:24,626
She thinks you and Hwal-sung
are behind the kidnapping.

594
00:34:26,211 --> 00:34:27,086
What?

595
00:34:27,087 --> 00:34:29,046
But it was you two who did that!

596
00:34:29,047 --> 00:34:30,381
I know.

597
00:34:30,382 --> 00:34:33,510
But how can I explain everything
to her face?

598
00:34:33,802 --> 00:34:35,844
I told her it was absolutely not you.

599
00:34:35,845 --> 00:34:36,804
Jeez!

600
00:34:36,805 --> 00:34:38,639
You should've said it more clearly!

601
00:34:38,640 --> 00:34:39,723
Seon,

602
00:34:39,724 --> 00:34:41,184
just listen to me, okay?

603
00:34:42,519 --> 00:34:44,728
It was Hwal-sung
who made us do it, okay?

604
00:34:44,729 --> 00:34:47,315
Say you don't know who did the kidnapping.

605
00:34:47,982 --> 00:34:48,482
Right.

606
00:34:48,483 --> 00:34:51,194
Let's say we had no idea
about the kidnapping, okay?

607
00:34:51,695 --> 00:34:53,196
What?

608
00:34:53,780 --> 00:34:55,489
I mean, what good is it
in making this a bigger deal?

609
00:34:55,490 --> 00:34:58,993
If I show up here, what good is that?
It just complicates things.

610
00:34:59,953 --> 00:35:01,203
First of all,

611
00:35:01,204 --> 00:35:03,080
Yi-gyeong trusts you more than Hwal-sung.

612
00:35:03,081 --> 00:35:04,206
Honestly speaking,

613
00:35:04,207 --> 00:35:06,501
would she do something bad to Da-rae?

614
00:35:06,918 --> 00:35:08,962
Seriously, what are you saying?

615
00:35:09,546 --> 00:35:12,090
Seon, let's just think about Da-rae.

616
00:35:29,566 --> 00:35:30,608
Where is Da-rae?

617
00:35:31,693 --> 00:35:34,529
Before you see Da-rae,
don't we have some things to sort out?

618
00:35:37,782 --> 00:35:38,950
I-I'm sorry.

619
00:35:39,951 --> 00:35:42,370
I was just helping
because Hwal-sung asked me.

620
00:35:43,246 --> 00:35:44,997
I didn't even know who I was kidnapping.

621
00:35:44,998 --> 00:35:47,875
If I had known it was you, I definitely
wouldn't have gone through with it.

622
00:35:47,876 --> 00:35:49,501
Yi-gyeong,
this was truly a mistake.

623
00:35:49,502 --> 00:35:51,879
Seon really didn't know anything.

624
00:35:51,880 --> 00:35:52,964
It's true.

625
00:35:54,424 --> 00:35:56,551
So, you did it together with my husband?

626
00:36:05,018 --> 00:36:07,186
You're going
to get blindsided.

627
00:36:07,187 --> 00:36:08,605
Just sitting around,
you'll become the sucker.

628
00:36:09,522 --> 00:36:10,899
You need to prepare for divorce too.

629
00:36:21,451 --> 00:36:23,619
You know about
the crimes Su-jong committed.

630
00:36:23,620 --> 00:36:26,164
Kidnapping Yi-gyeong, plus Oh Dong-ki

631
00:36:27,248 --> 00:36:28,416
and my mother-in-law's murder.

632
00:36:29,167 --> 00:36:31,085
We need to get a solid grip on this.

633
00:36:32,670 --> 00:36:33,713
I'll help you.

634
00:36:37,383 --> 00:36:38,802
I didn't see you that way,

635
00:36:39,803 --> 00:36:41,805
but your love for your husband
is surprisingly strong.

636
00:36:42,388 --> 00:36:45,141
Why are you
trying to take the blame?

637
00:36:45,892 --> 00:36:47,601
But what can I do?

638
00:36:47,602 --> 00:36:49,312
Your husband betrayed you.

639
00:36:49,813 --> 00:36:52,690
He told me you and Hwal-sung kidnapped me.

640
00:36:53,733 --> 00:36:56,528
I thought it was just an affair
or something.

641
00:36:56,945 --> 00:36:59,154
Then suddenly,
you said you were the kidnapper.

642
00:36:59,155 --> 00:36:59,948
What did he say?

643
00:37:00,865 --> 00:37:02,533
That you are Da-rae's mom

644
00:37:02,534 --> 00:37:05,035
and to please forgive you.

645
00:37:05,036 --> 00:37:05,829
Right?

646
00:37:13,294 --> 00:37:14,420
Yi-gyeong...

647
00:37:16,214 --> 00:37:18,549
There's a misunderstanding
about your mother.

648
00:37:18,550 --> 00:37:19,884
- It wasn't us...
- Seon.

649
00:37:21,177 --> 00:37:24,180
Don't you remember
what you said at my mom's funeral?

650
00:37:25,682 --> 00:37:27,392
How can you be so shameless?

651
00:37:28,518 --> 00:37:30,936
Su-jong and Hwal-sung may be trash,

652
00:37:30,937 --> 00:37:32,522
but I remember your words more clearly.

653
00:37:33,356 --> 00:37:35,233
You knew everything from the start.

654
00:37:36,150 --> 00:37:38,403
You treated me like a fool,
knowing all this!

655
00:37:39,153 --> 00:37:40,488
Doesn't that seem

656
00:37:40,989 --> 00:37:42,156
ridiculous to you?

657
00:37:48,371 --> 00:37:50,123
Let's end the truth game here.

658
00:37:54,919 --> 00:37:56,712
I'm sorry, Yi-gyeong.

659
00:37:56,713 --> 00:37:58,423
I really messed up.

660
00:37:59,090 --> 00:38:00,507
For Da-rae's sake,

661
00:38:00,508 --> 00:38:01,885
let's stop here.

662
00:38:02,677 --> 00:38:04,846
Da-rae got into Harvard.

663
00:38:05,680 --> 00:38:08,266
You said you wanted to invest
in Da-rae too.

664
00:38:12,854 --> 00:38:14,146
For Da-rae's sake,

665
00:38:14,147 --> 00:38:17,442
just once, please.

666
00:38:22,447 --> 00:38:23,948
What I want is simple.

667
00:38:25,116 --> 00:38:27,994
Both of you admit everything
and confess to the police.

668
00:38:28,578 --> 00:38:30,330
And transfer
the Seyoon Building shares to me.

669
00:38:32,040 --> 00:38:33,666
Then you don't have to worry about Da-rae.

670
00:38:34,876 --> 00:38:36,628
I'm cleaner than both of you

671
00:38:37,211 --> 00:38:38,046
to Da-rae.

672
00:38:40,548 --> 00:38:42,216
It's over. Just admit it.

673
00:38:45,261 --> 00:38:46,220
Yi-gyeong,

674
00:38:46,971 --> 00:38:48,181
I'll do anything.

675
00:38:48,389 --> 00:38:50,558
Let's leave Da-rae out of this
and just talk between us.

676
00:38:52,727 --> 00:38:53,811
Yi-gyeong...

677
00:39:20,713 --> 00:39:21,464
- Da-rae!
- Da-rae!

678
00:39:22,674 --> 00:39:23,257
Da-rae.

679
00:39:24,717 --> 00:39:25,677
Let's untie this.

680
00:39:35,103 --> 00:39:36,396
My gosh.

681
00:39:38,940 --> 00:39:40,315
Da-rae,

682
00:39:40,316 --> 00:39:41,359
are you hurt anywhere?

683
00:39:42,360 --> 00:39:43,528
I'm sorry.

684
00:39:44,570 --> 00:39:46,238
I'm tired...

685
00:39:46,239 --> 00:39:47,115
Yes.

686
00:39:47,490 --> 00:39:48,783
Da-rae, I'm sorry.

687
00:39:49,951 --> 00:39:52,996
Shouldn't you
apologize to her instead?

688
00:39:54,747 --> 00:39:56,081
I know.

689
00:39:56,082 --> 00:39:57,583
I'll definitely do that.

690
00:39:58,084 --> 00:39:59,752
Just hang in there, okay?

691
00:40:00,169 --> 00:40:01,671
I'm really sorry.

692
00:40:08,594 --> 00:40:10,596
My name is Kim Seon.

693
00:40:12,932 --> 00:40:14,767
I admit to assisting my husband,
Gi Su-jong,

694
00:40:15,893 --> 00:40:18,562
in the kidnapping of Jeon Yi-gyeong

695
00:40:18,563 --> 00:40:21,149
and obstructing the investigation.

696
00:40:22,608 --> 00:40:24,694
In addition, I confined Oh Dong-ki,

697
00:40:26,237 --> 00:40:29,114
and concerning the facts surrounding
Jeon Yang-ja's death,

698
00:40:29,115 --> 00:40:30,366
I also admit

699
00:40:30,950 --> 00:40:32,035
to covering them up.

700
00:40:33,786 --> 00:40:34,662
Yes.

701
00:40:41,419 --> 00:40:42,961
Jeon Yi-gyeong's abduction

702
00:40:42,962 --> 00:40:46,132
was the result of the actions of
Min Hwal-sung and I, Gi Su-jong.

703
00:40:48,176 --> 00:40:49,469
Oh Dong-ki's confinement

704
00:40:50,053 --> 00:40:52,805
was solely my doing. I also

705
00:40:53,264 --> 00:40:56,058
killed Jeon Yi-gyeong's husband,
Min Hwal-sung,

706
00:40:56,059 --> 00:40:58,269
and admit to disposing of the body.

707
00:41:00,813 --> 00:41:02,315
What is this about?

708
00:41:02,899 --> 00:41:03,858
Yi-gyeong,

709
00:41:04,984 --> 00:41:06,027
I'll just say

710
00:41:06,903 --> 00:41:07,904
one last thing.

711
00:41:08,362 --> 00:41:09,113
Honey.

712
00:41:09,530 --> 00:41:10,490
Seon,

713
00:41:11,157 --> 00:41:12,408
this is all my responsibility.

714
00:41:12,742 --> 00:41:13,534
I admit it.

715
00:41:14,410 --> 00:41:15,703
I'm sorry for lying.

716
00:41:16,454 --> 00:41:17,663
I thought

717
00:41:19,248 --> 00:41:21,334
I was doing it for my family.
I was such a fool.

718
00:41:22,502 --> 00:41:24,377
So please just give me

719
00:41:24,378 --> 00:41:26,130
one last chance to turn back.

720
00:41:27,381 --> 00:41:28,715
Yi-gyeong,

721
00:41:28,716 --> 00:41:29,842
I'm truly sorry.

722
00:41:30,718 --> 00:41:32,970
I know it's hard to understand
and I can't turn it back.

723
00:41:33,346 --> 00:41:36,056
I'm not asking for your forgiveness.

724
00:41:36,057 --> 00:41:38,851
I'll go to prison.
I'll take responsibility. I just ask

725
00:41:39,268 --> 00:41:41,478
that you please help Da-rae and her mom

726
00:41:41,479 --> 00:41:43,313
live as best

727
00:41:43,314 --> 00:41:44,232
as they can.

728
00:41:44,857 --> 00:41:46,233
For these two,

729
00:41:46,234 --> 00:41:48,111
their only crime is having me

730
00:41:48,861 --> 00:41:50,738
as a husband and a father.

731
00:41:51,405 --> 00:41:53,658
Yi-gyeong, please give me a chance.

732
00:41:54,033 --> 00:41:56,327
I'm giving you enough chances.

733
00:41:57,161 --> 00:41:58,079
Yes.

734
00:41:58,913 --> 00:42:00,414
Yi-gyeong, about Pyeong-buk Gwan,

735
00:42:01,040 --> 00:42:03,501
Min Hwal-sung conspired
with Attorney Yang to fix the documents

736
00:42:04,001 --> 00:42:05,711
so that you are unable to do anything.

737
00:42:06,587 --> 00:42:08,421
The rest of your mother's estate,

738
00:42:08,422 --> 00:42:10,382
Hwal-sung probably placed them

739
00:42:10,383 --> 00:42:11,384
in his name.

740
00:42:12,969 --> 00:42:13,803
So what?

741
00:42:15,555 --> 00:42:18,516
The start of all this is Min Hwal-sung.

742
00:42:18,975 --> 00:42:21,144
I'll settle the score.

743
00:42:22,520 --> 00:42:23,563
Tonight,

744
00:42:24,147 --> 00:42:26,399
I'll kill Min Hwal-sung and go to jail.

745
00:42:27,316 --> 00:42:28,776
I'll go to the police
and confess.

746
00:42:29,819 --> 00:42:30,653
I'll testify too.

747
00:42:31,195 --> 00:42:32,780
I'll even transfer my shares.

748
00:42:33,197 --> 00:42:35,949
Then wouldn't it all
end perfectly for you?

749
00:42:35,950 --> 00:42:36,909
And get your revenge too.

750
00:42:37,952 --> 00:42:40,370
Just please leave

751
00:42:40,371 --> 00:42:43,123
only the Seyoon Building to Seon.
I'm begging you.

752
00:42:43,124 --> 00:42:45,585
Honey, what are you doing?
Are you out of your mind?

753
00:42:46,294 --> 00:42:47,545
I need to put things back together.

754
00:42:48,171 --> 00:42:49,881
Min Hwal-sung and I
just need to disappear.

755
00:42:51,924 --> 00:42:52,842
Seon,

756
00:42:53,384 --> 00:42:55,052
does this even make sense?

757
00:42:56,596 --> 00:42:58,806
Yi-gyeong, before I go to jail,

758
00:42:59,974 --> 00:43:01,309
if I kill Hwal-sung,

759
00:43:02,268 --> 00:43:04,020
it's all over. It's finished.

760
00:43:25,249 --> 00:43:26,584
I'm in front of
Gi Su-jong's house.

761
00:43:29,587 --> 00:43:30,713
What do you think?

762
00:43:31,380 --> 00:43:33,882
Killing people
is not something anyone can do.

763
00:43:33,883 --> 00:43:35,301
He's just messing around.

764
00:43:36,469 --> 00:43:37,636
Watch closely.

765
00:43:37,637 --> 00:43:38,804
If he does something stupid, bring him in.

766
00:43:40,264 --> 00:43:41,015
Okay.

767
00:43:43,392 --> 00:43:44,227
MS. YI-GYEONG

768
00:44:04,705 --> 00:44:06,457
What were you thinking?

769
00:44:06,916 --> 00:44:08,542
Were you really planning
to kill Hwal-sung?

770
00:44:09,043 --> 00:44:11,253
Do you remember when you told me

771
00:44:11,254 --> 00:44:14,465
you could kill and revivesomeone like in Romeo and Juliet?

772
00:44:15,758 --> 00:44:17,092
Actually, Juliet

773
00:44:17,093 --> 00:44:19,719
didn't die from drinking poison.

774
00:44:19,720 --> 00:44:22,472
She took a sleep-inducing drug
that temporarily

775
00:44:22,473 --> 00:44:24,724
slowed her heartbeat and breathing.

776
00:44:24,725 --> 00:44:26,769
Hey, does that
really make sense?

777
00:44:27,144 --> 00:44:29,854
With anesthesia and
the right tools, it's not that hard.

778
00:44:29,855 --> 00:44:30,815
Really?

779
00:44:32,441 --> 00:44:34,485
Listen, here's my plan.

780
00:44:35,695 --> 00:44:37,946
You contact Ae-su and get

781
00:44:37,947 --> 00:44:40,616
- the necessary anesthetics and tools.
- I have a request,

782
00:44:41,158 --> 00:44:42,201
Can you talk on the phone?

783
00:44:57,883 --> 00:45:00,760
And when you call
Min Hwal-sung,

784
00:45:00,761 --> 00:45:04,932
I'll knock him out with a stun gun
and kidnap him.

785
00:45:05,891 --> 00:45:06,809
Wow, this works.

786
00:45:07,852 --> 00:45:10,146
I know an abandoned building.

787
00:45:12,064 --> 00:45:15,151
We'll fake an accident
for that guy with the sunglasses,

788
00:45:15,901 --> 00:45:17,653
then we'll head
to that abandoned building.

789
00:45:19,322 --> 00:45:20,406
Wait a second.

790
00:45:20,865 --> 00:45:22,867
Can a death from falling
happen in an abandoned place?

791
00:45:23,117 --> 00:45:24,701
That's true, but...

792
00:45:24,702 --> 00:45:27,246
if you go there, it'll make sense.

793
00:45:28,831 --> 00:45:31,916
There, you give
Min Hwal-sung the injection

794
00:45:31,917 --> 00:45:34,169
and after we pretended to kill him,

795
00:45:34,170 --> 00:45:36,921
we'll ask that sunglasses guy for help
in throwing off the body.

796
00:45:36,922 --> 00:45:38,966
After luring him in.
we zap him with the stun gun!

797
00:45:43,262 --> 00:45:45,973
While Min Hwal-sung is dead,
we get him to stamp the contract.

798
00:45:50,686 --> 00:45:51,436
After that,

799
00:45:51,437 --> 00:45:53,313
we revive Min Hwal-sung.

800
00:45:53,314 --> 00:45:53,856
What do you think?

801
00:45:57,234 --> 00:45:58,069
It's possible,

802
00:45:58,486 --> 00:45:59,820
if we bring him back within four minutes.

803
00:46:02,281 --> 00:46:03,157
Four minutes.

804
00:46:03,574 --> 00:46:04,450
Maximum of five minutes.

805
00:46:04,742 --> 00:46:06,659
But if you make even a small mistake,
it's over.

806
00:46:06,660 --> 00:46:07,703
Can you do it?

807
00:46:09,413 --> 00:46:10,331
I can do it.

808
00:46:14,668 --> 00:46:16,045
Yi-gyeong is pregnant.

809
00:46:16,545 --> 00:46:17,296
What?

810
00:46:19,548 --> 00:46:20,674
You're a dad now.

811
00:46:43,656 --> 00:46:45,825
Sir, how old is your child?

812
00:46:46,200 --> 00:46:49,120
Oh, still in the womb.

813
00:46:50,496 --> 00:46:53,373
Um, do you have
newborn supplies too?

814
00:46:53,374 --> 00:46:55,500
Yes, this section
has all the newborn items.

815
00:46:55,501 --> 00:46:56,042
I see.

816
00:46:56,043 --> 00:46:58,503
And over here,
many people look for bloomers too.

817
00:46:58,504 --> 00:47:00,714
Oh, bloomers...

818
00:47:03,384 --> 00:47:04,385
This...

819
00:47:09,723 --> 00:47:12,017
I'll give you this one
as a freebie.

820
00:47:13,936 --> 00:47:15,645
Congratulations on becoming a dad.

821
00:47:15,646 --> 00:47:16,564
Thank you.

822
00:47:17,898 --> 00:47:19,316
Um,

823
00:47:19,859 --> 00:47:22,110
is there something good for moms?

824
00:47:22,111 --> 00:47:23,736
Iron and magnesium.

825
00:47:23,737 --> 00:47:25,239
- I can recommend some supplements.
- Oh, sure.

826
00:47:30,411 --> 00:47:32,872
KIM SEON

827
00:47:33,414 --> 00:47:34,748
Hold on a second.

828
00:47:37,793 --> 00:47:38,544
Hello?

829
00:47:39,086 --> 00:47:40,087
Where are you?

830
00:47:40,713 --> 00:47:42,131
Can we meet for a minute?

831
00:47:42,715 --> 00:47:43,799
It'll be tough.

832
00:47:44,717 --> 00:47:46,886
You should focus on your family now.

833
00:47:47,928 --> 00:47:48,761
What?

834
00:47:48,762 --> 00:47:51,140
Seon, don't call me anymore.

835
00:47:51,932 --> 00:47:52,975
It'll be hard,

836
00:47:53,684 --> 00:47:55,143
but let's keep our relationship
in our memories.

837
00:47:55,144 --> 00:47:56,312
Damn it.

838
00:47:57,229 --> 00:47:59,482
Stop saying weird things
and let's meet for a moment.

839
00:47:59,690 --> 00:48:00,774
I have something to sort out.

840
00:48:03,527 --> 00:48:04,861
Is this really the last time?

841
00:48:04,862 --> 00:48:05,612
Yes.

842
00:48:05,613 --> 00:48:06,780
I'll head that way.

843
00:48:08,073 --> 00:48:08,741
MIN HWAL-SUNG

844
00:48:09,783 --> 00:48:11,118
Memories?

845
00:48:11,327 --> 00:48:12,453
It's just nonsense.

846
00:48:12,661 --> 00:48:14,121
We don't know about that.

847
00:48:14,288 --> 00:48:15,498
Stop it.

848
00:48:15,748 --> 00:48:17,374
This could be true love for this jerk.

849
00:48:18,501 --> 00:48:19,585
Shut up.

850
00:48:21,003 --> 00:48:22,213
I've arrived.

851
00:48:49,615 --> 00:48:52,034
Then I'll handle
a certain amount.

852
00:48:55,120 --> 00:48:56,121
Is that a man or a woman?

853
00:49:00,167 --> 00:49:01,085
Let's go.

854
00:50:03,522 --> 00:50:05,733
Hwal-sung!

855
00:50:15,701 --> 00:50:16,910
What's this car about?

856
00:50:39,975 --> 00:50:41,226
We got Min Hwal-sung.

857
00:51:00,412 --> 00:51:02,164
- Are you really going to do it?
- Yes.

858
00:52:03,225 --> 00:52:06,520
EXERCISING THE RIGHT TO CLAIM

859
00:52:51,607 --> 00:52:53,776
Hold on, who is this?

860
00:52:55,486 --> 00:52:57,571
W-Why are you doing this to me?

861
00:52:59,114 --> 00:53:01,283
Hold on...

862
00:53:09,708 --> 00:53:11,293
W-What are you guys doing?

863
00:53:12,753 --> 00:53:13,587
Hwal-sung,

864
00:53:14,296 --> 00:53:15,631
you're going to die today.

865
00:53:18,926 --> 00:53:19,802
What?

866
00:53:21,720 --> 00:53:22,638
What do you mean by that?

867
00:53:29,019 --> 00:53:30,520
Hey, hey...

868
00:53:30,521 --> 00:53:31,145
Hey!

869
00:53:31,146 --> 00:53:32,688
Hey, are you crazy?

870
00:53:32,689 --> 00:53:34,357
Seon, tell him to stop!

871
00:53:34,358 --> 00:53:35,066
Hey, wait a second!

872
00:53:35,067 --> 00:53:36,400
Hey, who told you to do this?

873
00:53:36,401 --> 00:53:37,193
Who ordered you?

874
00:53:37,194 --> 00:53:39,403
- Was it Mr. Nam? Huh?
- What a sight this is.

875
00:53:39,404 --> 00:53:40,613
Was it Hee-ju?

876
00:53:40,614 --> 00:53:41,990
This show is really entertaining.

877
00:53:43,700 --> 00:53:45,160
Just keep watching.

878
00:53:59,925 --> 00:54:02,845
Hey, do you know
how Mr. Nam and Hee-ju are connected?

879
00:54:03,220 --> 00:54:06,472
Those two were trying to push you aside
and steal the business.

880
00:54:06,473 --> 00:54:08,433
I stopped that!

881
00:54:09,393 --> 00:54:10,936
Did you meet Hee-ju last night?

882
00:54:12,062 --> 00:54:13,438
No, I just talked to her on the phone.

883
00:54:14,064 --> 00:54:17,692
She recorded
and took pictures of you to send.

884
00:54:17,693 --> 00:54:19,528
I stopped her while on the phone.

885
00:54:20,028 --> 00:54:24,365
But still, it would be better
for you to come to me

886
00:54:24,366 --> 00:54:26,076
rather than going to that
Nam Sang-ho bastard.

887
00:54:26,326 --> 00:54:27,411
What time did you call?

888
00:54:28,662 --> 00:54:30,163
Around 2 AM.

889
00:54:36,420 --> 00:54:37,713
Is that enough?
Hey, wait a second.

890
00:54:37,838 --> 00:54:39,172
Let me go, okay?

891
00:54:39,965 --> 00:54:40,841
Hey.

892
00:54:41,425 --> 00:54:43,634
Hey, how does killing me

893
00:54:43,635 --> 00:54:45,345
solve anything?

894
00:54:47,097 --> 00:54:49,433
If you hadn't done
the kidnapping back then,

895
00:54:50,893 --> 00:54:52,936
we wouldn't have come this far.

896
00:54:57,149 --> 00:54:59,276
I know.

897
00:55:00,152 --> 00:55:00,944
Hey,

898
00:55:02,070 --> 00:55:03,322
I really thought if I just

899
00:55:04,114 --> 00:55:07,075
kept Yi-gyeong captive for a bit,
things would be resolved.

900
00:55:07,618 --> 00:55:10,078
You know I really needed that money.

901
00:55:11,204 --> 00:55:12,664
If I had that money,

902
00:55:13,248 --> 00:55:15,249
then

903
00:55:15,250 --> 00:55:17,836
my mother-in-law
would have acknowledged me.

904
00:55:18,629 --> 00:55:21,173
I really want to make it work
with Yi-gyeong.

905
00:55:22,215 --> 00:55:24,051
It was my last resort.

906
00:55:25,969 --> 00:55:27,012
Hwal-sung,

907
00:55:27,930 --> 00:55:29,014
let's stop now.

908
00:55:29,514 --> 00:55:30,599
It's too late.

909
00:55:30,974 --> 00:55:32,183
Wait, hold on!

910
00:55:32,184 --> 00:55:34,352
Wait, wait! Okay!

911
00:55:34,353 --> 00:55:35,938
Okay! I get it!

912
00:55:37,940 --> 00:55:40,192
Take this out of my pocket

913
00:55:41,318 --> 00:55:42,694
and give it to Yi-gyeong.

914
00:56:01,380 --> 00:56:02,880
For our baby,

915
00:56:02,881 --> 00:56:04,800
just tell her the good things
about her dad.

916
00:56:06,802 --> 00:56:09,137
Don't tell her about
everything I've done, got it?

917
00:56:11,890 --> 00:56:12,808
Seon, let's do this.

918
00:56:21,483 --> 00:56:23,443
See you in hell, my friend.

919
00:56:40,627 --> 00:56:41,461
Oh.

920
00:56:42,421 --> 00:56:43,672
Did he really do it?

921
00:57:33,388 --> 00:57:36,308
Wow, they really killed him.

922
00:57:37,851 --> 00:57:38,851
He's dead.

923
00:57:38,852 --> 00:57:41,020
No! No!

924
00:57:41,021 --> 00:57:41,980
No way!

925
00:57:57,954 --> 00:57:59,748
I sent the photo.

926
00:58:08,548 --> 00:58:09,341
Hello?

927
00:58:11,343 --> 00:58:12,552
He really is dead.

928
00:58:31,696 --> 00:58:32,447
Excuse me.

929
00:58:33,115 --> 00:58:33,990
Just a second.

930
00:58:42,999 --> 00:58:43,875
Listen.

931
00:58:45,877 --> 00:58:46,920
We planned on

932
00:58:47,337 --> 00:58:49,005
making it seem like

933
00:58:49,589 --> 00:58:52,383
he came to check out an auction item
and ended up falling.

934
00:58:52,384 --> 00:58:54,218
Just help us carry him to that spot.

935
00:58:54,219 --> 00:58:55,220
Jeez.

936
00:58:58,098 --> 00:58:59,933
Making me do everything.

937
00:59:12,028 --> 00:59:12,821
What is this?

938
00:59:18,577 --> 00:59:19,619
What are you guys doing?

939
00:59:22,873 --> 00:59:25,125
Don't come near.

940
00:59:25,750 --> 00:59:26,959
What?

941
00:59:26,960 --> 00:59:27,878
Don't come near!

942
00:59:29,045 --> 00:59:29,796
What are you doing?

943
01:00:19,095 --> 01:00:21,014
SPECIAL THANKS TO ACTOR KIM NAM-GIL

944
01:00:37,113 --> 01:00:40,199
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

945
01:00:40,200 --> 01:00:41,367
Hey, Gi Su-jong!

946
01:00:41,368 --> 01:00:42,494
Seon, run away!

947
01:00:42,869 --> 01:00:43,578
Gi Su-jong?

948
01:00:43,787 --> 01:00:45,079
What about Gi Su-jong?

949
01:00:45,080 --> 01:00:46,664
Don't stir things up without evidence!

950
01:00:46,665 --> 01:00:47,582
Shall we go?

951
01:00:47,749 --> 01:00:49,792
Please come
to Seyoon Building right now.

952
01:00:49,793 --> 01:00:52,295
The suspect that you want to catch
is right here.

953
01:00:52,587 --> 01:00:53,587
Honey,

954
01:00:53,588 --> 01:00:54,631
what do we do now?

955
01:00:54,881 --> 01:00:58,759
Didn't Min Hwal-sung
leave some last words?

956
01:00:58,760 --> 01:01:00,553
Please, just stop!

957
01:01:00,887 --> 01:01:03,265
Your parents are the ones
who crossed the line first.

958
01:01:03,556 --> 01:01:06,058
Don't come near! Stay away!

959
01:01:06,059 --> 01:01:06,935
Don't come!

